,""]}],[{"headerIndex":399,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":402,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":404,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"Man"],"rowInfoText":"Man"}],[{"headerIndex":406,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":408,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"Man"],"rowInfoText":"Man"}],[{"headerIndex":410,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":412,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":414,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":416,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"Man"],"rowInfoText":"Man"}],[{"headerIndex":418,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":420,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":422,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":424,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"Man"],"rowInfoText":"Man"}],[{"headerIndex":426,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":428,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,"You"],"rowInfoText":"You"}],[{"headerIndex":431,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":433,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":435,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":441,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":443,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":445,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":447,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":449,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],[{"headerIndex":451,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}],null,null,null,[{"headerIndex":11,"headerParam":["",0,0,2,""]}]],"indexIds":{"ch 1 Final Hunt":0,"pls_open":1,"Game saved successfully in slot ":2,"Failed to save game:":3,"Chapter 1 : The Final Hunt":4,"forest_fire":5,"You step out of the worn-out house, the door creaking behind you as it swings shut.":6,"The weight of your gear drags at your body, but it’s not just the equipment — it’s the years.":7,"You’ve been preparing for this night longer than you care to admit. Every step feels heavy.":8,"But you can’t stop. Not now.":9,"Your gaze lingers on the windows. Inside, the shadows of your old life remain — a life that feels like a ghost now.":10,"Photographs on the walls, dust-covered remnants of forgotten hobbies. There was a time when you had dreams — other dreams. ":11,"But they’ve long since crumbled, replaced by a singular, consuming purpose: hunting.":12,"You hear it.":13,"Birds flapping in a hurried ascent. You know what that means. ":14,"Sunset is close.":15,"It's time.":16,"The bonfire pierces the encroaching darkness, a lone beacon amidst the towering trees. ":17,"You finish threading the barbed wire from tree to tree, building a harsh perimeter around the clearing — a trap with no escape. ":18,"Your gaze drifts toward the horizon as the sun sinks lower, disappearing behind the trees, casting long shadows that stretch like dark fingers clawing at the ground. ":19,"You need to be fast. They’ll come soon.":20,"Put tripwires outside the clearing as well":21,"Put tripwires only inside the clearing":22,"You extend the explosives beyond the clearing, placing tripwires along the outer perimeter. If any of them manage to slip past the first line of defense, these will catch them.":23,"Tonight, there’s no escape.":24,"They’ll be drawn to the bonfire like moths to a flame. Concentrating the explosives within the clearing will ensure they’re right where you want them when the trap springs. ":25,"The forest deepens into shadow as you finish setting the tripwires. You nod, satisfied — but there’s one last step.":26,"Pulling out a knife, you make a swift cut across your palm, letting your blood drip onto the soil. It’s dark, almost black in the fading light, and the ground drinks it up, vanishing as quickly as it falls.":27,"You wrap the wound with a strip of cloth, tightening it until the pain is just a dull throb.":28,"You don’t usually do this. They’re already drawn to the living.":29,"But today is different. You need all of them to come.":30,"You’ve tried tracking them to their lairs before, but the tunnels are too winding, too deep, too impossible to navigate. ":31,"So instead, you draw them out — just like they lure humans, using their scent to pull people to their deaths. ":32,"It’s a brutal contest of hunters, and you intend to be the last one standing. ":33,"Sliding the gas mask over your face, the rubber cool and constricting against your skin, you settle behind a tree.":34,"A sharp pang of isolation digs into you. You wish you didn’t have to do this alone, but the remaining townsfolk have… changed. ":35,"Consumed by whatever the creatures emit, they’ve become something else. Something hollow. You need to put a stop to this before they sacrifice someone else.":36,"The last rays of sunlight disappear, leaving a dense, suffocating silence. It’s as if the forest itself is holding its breath, aware of what’s coming.":37,"Your hands tremble slightly as you grip the flamethrower, its metal cold despite the sweat on your palms.":38,"As soon as the creatures step into the clearing, the explosives will rip through the first wave, and the barbed wire will hold the rest in place.":39,"Then more will come. You’ll pick them off, wave by wave, until nothing’s left but ash. ":40,"After all these years of hunting, it all comes down to this. Tonight, either you kill them all, or they finally take you.":41,"leon":42,"normal":43,"Leon drives into the city, the streets dead and abandoned — another ghost town, courtesy of Umbrella.":44,"Boarded windows, doors nailed shut, like they’re trying to keep something out. Or in.":45,"He wonders how many more are there. He thought that after Umbrella’s downfall, they had dealt with all of them. But every now and then another one pops up.":46,"He feels it — a prickle on the back of his neck. ":47,"His eyes flick to a cracked window as he passes, but there’s nothing there. Just shadows, shifting with the last light of day.":48,"Leon":49,"Hate it when the neighbors are this quiet.":50,"The sun sinks lower, bleeding orange and red across the sky. He sighs, tapping his fingers on the handlebars.":51,"He wanted to get here earlier, but the mission briefing dragged on, and the local cops weren’t exactly helpful. ":52,"When he asked if they’d seen anything strange, they all gave him the same blank stare. Nope. Nothing, sir.":53,"He’s not sure if they’re lying, clueless, or just terrified.":54,"His GPS flashes, guiding him toward the lab on the outskirts. It’s nestled in the forest, up on a hill. ":55,"Easy enough, right? Just find the missing team, check the lab, and get out.":56,"Simple.":57,"Except it never is.":58,"Leon kills the engine and swings off the bike, the silence wrapping around him. The air feels... wrong. Too still. The kind of stillness that gets under your skin.":59,"Okay, Leon. Just another spooky forest. What could go wrong?":60,"He moves on foot, the ground soft under his boots, dead leaves muffling his steps. His hand hovers near his gun. The path is narrow, overgrown, and the shadows stretch out long in the fading light.":61,"Then he sees it — a flickering light through the trees. ":62,"Leon stops, narrowing his eyes. Someone’s here. Maybe it’s the missing team. Or something else.":63,"He steps off the path, crouching low behind a tree for cover, watching the bonfire pulse in the dark.":64,"Whoever’s camping out here has terrible taste in ambiance. ":65,"Then a faint smell hits him — sweet, cloying, almost floral.":66,"angry":67,"He grips his gun tighter, muscles tensing as his instincts kick in. This isn’t the usual rotting stench of B.O.W.s. This is... different. Wrong. Whatever’s ahead, it feels like it’s calling to him.":68,"The last of the sunlight slips behind the trees. Darkness closes in, and the light flickers again, casting eerie shadows that seem to reach for him.":69,"He moves forward, slow and steady, his senses on high alert. He’s done this before, more times than he’d care to remember. ":70,"Whatever’s waiting in the dark, it’s not going to catch him off guard.":71,"Leon’s head is getting foggy, his senses dulled. He can see the fire now — a huge bonfire lighting up the dark.":72,"Spotting an opening, he steps forward, but something brushes against his chest — a wire.":73,"The faint beeping reaches him a second too late. ":74,"surp":75,"Guess I really walked into that one.":76,"The tripwire triggers, a deafening blast tearing through the air. ":77,"You listen, breath fogging the inside of your gas mask. The forest feels suffocating, every shadow pressing in, thick with tension.":78,"A sharp, creaking noise breaks the silence — the sound of chitinous legs scraping over dry bark. The familiar clicks and snaps you’ve come to associate with the creatures.":79,"They’re here.":80,"Your heart pounds, and you steady your breath, the filtered air dry and stale against your lips. ":81,"Fingers tightening around the flamethrower, you prepare to rise from your hiding spot, every muscle coiled.":82,"But then, movement catches your eye — a figure, slipping through the clearing. ":83,"A man.":84,"You freeze, watching as he steps closer to your traps.":85,"Wait. Is he…?":86,"He’s disabling your tripwires!":87,"Your pulse races, heart hammering in your ears. Without thinking, you sprint from your spot, weaving through the traps you’ve committed to memory.":88,"You":89,"You! Stop!":90,"Your voice comes out muffled, distorted by the mask, but he halts, turning to face you.":91,"For a split second, you’re taken aback. He’s... not what you expected. Sharp features, piercing eyes. Striking, in a way that seems out of place here.":92,"Not the kind of person you’d expect to stumble into a nightmare like this.":93,"Your gaze flicks to his hand — hovering near his gun, posture tense and controlled. Definitely not a civilian.":94,"What the hell do you think you’re doing?":95,"These traps are mine.":96,"eyebrow":97,"He raises an eyebrow, unbothered by your tone.":98,"Man":99,"These are yours?":100,"Yes.":101,"I’d appreciate it if you didn’t mess with them. ":102,"He glances around at the scattered wires, looking almost amused.":103,"Oh. My bad.":104,"How many did you disable already?":105,"He tilts his head, thinking for a moment. ":106,"A… few.":107,"You curse under your breath, gripping the flamethrower tighter. Just your luck — a clueless outsider ruining the day you’ve waited years for.":108,"Why do you need so many explosives?":109,"I’m hunting.":110,"His eyes shift to the flamethrower in your hands, then to the barbed wire strung between trees. ":111,"You have a rather… unconventional way of hunting.":112,"You take a steadying breath. No time for this.":113,"You’re not from this town, are you? You really should leave. Now.":114,"Your gaze drifts to the treeline, where you sense movement. The scent is starting to seep in, that sickly-sweet, floral odor the creatures emit.":115,"He’s not wearing a mask — already, you see a slight daze in his eyes. He won’t last long if they get too close.":116,"The man shakes his head, taking a step closer.":117,"Not an option. I’ve got to get to that lab, and this is the only way through.":118,"You fidget with the flamethrower, torn between curiosity and frustration. Whoever he is, he needs to leave.":119,"You have no idea what’s out there. Turn around. Wait until morning. Whatever you’re looking for at the lab — it’s already been ransacked.":120,"But do whatever you want, just not right now.":121,"A familiar sound echoes through the forest — the same clicking, the same sickening creak. They’re getting closer. He hears it too, his stance shifting, eyes narrowing. ":122,"What exactly are you hunting?":123,"Before you can respond, yellow eyes blink to life at the edge of the woods. Dozens of them, gleaming like fireflies in the dark, shifting as they lock onto you.":124,"There are more than you expected, likely drawn by his scent as well. You can’t fight them all without the explosives.":125,"Run.":126,"You don’t wait for his response. Explosions erupt, the ground shaking underfoot, but the creatures charge through the smoke, faster than you anticipated.":127,"You dash forward, dodging traps, weaving through the maze of wires and explosives. ":128,"Gunshots ring out behind you. You glance back, catching sight of him — firing at the creatures as he runs, somehow keeping pace. ":129,"Save your bullets! It won't kill them!":130,"A sharp crack sounds, and suddenly, warm air seeps into the mask. A piece of debris must have punctured it.":131,"You’re exposed now, no spare within reach. You can only keep running.":132,"Barreling through the underbrush, you fire the flamethrower behind you, a wave of fire scorching the air. The creatures shriek and stumble back, but keep coming.":133,"You see him aim, shooting one of the explosives rigged to a nearby tree. ":134,"The explosion rocks the clearing, and smoke blankets everything, the forest erupting into chaos. ":135,"You run until you’re far away, gasping as you tear off the broken mask.":136,"The cool night air fills your lungs, but it feels like failure. Everything you built is gone. The traps, the explosives — all of it, wasted.":137,"The man catches up, glancing back at the smoke and fire flickering in the distance. His gun is still in hand, and he looks... unfazed.":138,"Quite the fireworks show back there.":139,"He looks at you, raising an eyebrow. ":140,"What were those things? You’ve fought them before, right? ":141,"Your blood boils, and you throw the broken mask to the ground. ":142,"It’s your fault":143,"It’s his fault":144,"You should’ve kept going. Should’ve stuck with the plan and ignored the outsider. Your fury fades, giving way to a hollow sense of defeat. ":145,"I prepared for this day for a long time. I was going to kill all of them.":146,"There’s no way you could’ve taken them all down on your own.":147,"You shake your head, chuckling low as tears prickle at your eyes. You have no energy left to argue. ":148,"Right. I should’ve know. I’ve already failed so many people… what’s one more mistake? ":149,"Look, I didn’t mean to mess things up— ":150,"It’s all your fault!":151,"What?":152,"I was going to kill every last one of them. I had everything set. And you ruined it. You ruined everything! ":153,"He takes a defensive stance, eyes hardening. ":154,"Hey, I didn’t know you had that place rigged to explode. Maybe next time, leave a sign.":155,"You glare back at him.":156,"Leave, outsider, before you mess things up even further. It’s not safe here.":157,"He narrows his eyes, looking at you with a calm that only makes your frustration flare hotter.":158,"Not for me. For you. You’re going to get yourself killed if you keep this up.":159,"Excuse me? You’re the one who almost got yourself killed back there.":160,"I’m trained for this. I can handle it.":161,"You don’t know these things like I do. They lure you with their scent.":162,"You want to get to the lab now? Go ahead. But you’ll end up like everyone else who’s tried — dead.":163,"He pauses, and for the first time, you see his expression soften slightly as he studies you. ":164,"Did you see a team come through here?":165,"A lot of people come through here. They go to the lab, they get what they want, and they leave us to our fate.":166,"Or they go and never come back. Whoever you’re looking for — they’re probably dead. Or worse.":167,"The man looks back toward the forest, his expression turning somber, thoughtful.":168,"I need to go to the lab and figure out what happened to them. I’m not leaving until I do.":169,"You shake your head, unsurprised. Of course. They’re all the same. ":170,"Good luck. You'll need it.":171,"Without waiting for a response, you turn and march away, ignoring the ache in your chest. You’ll have to start all over again — rebuild, rearm.":172,"Your hand finds the pendant resting against your chest. You grip it tightly, letting the familiar shape press into your skin.":173,"I’m sorry.":174,"You storm back to the house, slamming the door behind you.":175,"The gear drops from your hands, but you barely notice. All you can think about is him — the arrogant outsider with his stoic face.":176,"You grit your teeth. He’s going to get himself killed. You know it. He doesn’t even have a mask. The second he gets close to the lab, he’s as good as dead.":177,"You told him to leave, warned him what was out there. If he dies, that’s on him. You owe him nothing. He ruined your plan, your final chance at saving the rest of this town.":178,"But the thought of him stumbling into the lab, clueless, gnaws at you. Why the hell do you care? You shouldn’t.":179,"You don’t.":180,"skin_choice":181,"Linear":182,"Unchanged":183,"Choose a skin color:":184,"White <Bind Picture: 50>":185,"Brown <Bind Picture: 51>":186,"Black <Bind Picture: 52>":187,"<Hide Choice Window> ":188},"extension":"json","dataType":"map","filename":"Map004","basename":"Map004.json","path":"data/Map004.json","relPath":"data/Map004.json","dirname":"/data","originalFormat":"RPG MAKER MV RAW DATA","lineBreak":"\n","type":"","indexIsBuilt":true,"progress":{"translated":0,"length":189,"percent":0},"cacheResetOnChange":{},"cellInfo":[[null,{"t":"HU","v":1},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[null,{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"},{"t":"HU"}],[